<title>NETHERLANDS: Port of Rotterdam turnover falls 0.5 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Port of Rotterdam turnover falls 0.5 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>ROTTERDAM 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Port of Rotterdam turnover in 1996 fell 0.5 percent to 292.0 million tonnes from 1995's record 293.4 million tonnes, according to the port's final 1996 figures.</p>
<p>			  1996	   PCT YR/YR CHANGE</p>
<p> All cargo	    292.0	     -0.5</p>
<p> Agribulk		13.2	    -14.7</p>
<p> Ores and scrap	39.8	    -14.0</p>
<p> Coal		    18.5	     +3.2</p>
<p> Other dry bulk	12.4	    +24.8</p>
<p> Total dry bulk	83.9	     -6.4</p>
<p> Crude oil	    100.2	     +4.0</p>
<p> Oil products	  13.9	    -16.6</p>
<p> Other liquid bulk   22.0	    +11.0</p>
<p> Total liquid bulk  136.1	     +2.5</p>
<p> Roll-on/Roll-off     8.5	     +5.4</p>
<p> Containers	    53.4	     +2.0</p>
<p> Other general cargo 10.1	     -3.7</p>
<p> Total general cargo 72.0	     +1.5</p>
<p>NOTE: In its provisional figures in December, the port put the overall fall at 0.9 percent.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
